          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mrx77cdxgqu9590h",
          "message": {
            "text": "Two subtleties in the detection predicate: (1) the comparison uses the NEW `SessionState.resolvedCommand` (captured at spawn, pre-shell-history-rewrite) rather than `session.command` — the rewrite wraps the resolved command in a history-scoping shim, so comparing the rewritten form against a fresh resolution would always differ and the chip would never turn off. (2) The `fresh.includes(attach)` clause is the scope guard: \"fresh differs from launch\" alone would also fire on unrelated terminal-config/template edits; requiring the fresh resolution to contain the current attach command limits the signal to codex-attach drift in both directions (plain→attach-available and attached→stale-after-reset), including template expansions like `env X=1 <attach>`. The action side needs no new server path — `POST /terminal/restart` already re-resolves on spawn, which is exactly the relaunch semantics.\n",
            "markdown": "Two subtleties in the detection predicate: (1) the comparison uses the NEW `SessionState.resolvedCommand` (captured at spawn, pre-shell-history-rewrite) rather than `session.command` — the rewrite wraps the resolved command in a history-scoping shim, so comparing the rewritten form against a fresh resolution would always differ and the chip would never turn off. (2) The `fresh.includes(attach)` clause is the scope guard: \"fresh differs from launch\" alone would also fire on unrelated terminal-config/template edits; requiring the fresh resolution to contain the current attach command limits the signal to codex-attach drift in both directions (plain→attach-available and attached→stale-after-reset), including template expansions like `env X=1 <attach>`. The action side needs no new server path — `POST /terminal/restart` already re-resolves on spawn, which is exactly the relaunch semantics.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/terminals/codexReattach.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 29,
                  "endLine": 43,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function codexReattachAvailable(secret: string, dataDir: string, terminalId: string, deps: CodexReattachDeps = {}): boolean {\n  const session = sessions.get(sessionKey(secret, terminalId));\n  if (session === undefined || session.pty === null || session.resolvedCommand === null) return false;\n  const attachCommand = deps.attachCommand ?? codexTerminalAttachCommand;\n  const attach = attachCommand(dataDir);\n  if (attach === null) return false;\n  const fresh = (deps.resolve ?? resolveTerminalCommand)({\n    dataDir,\n    terminalId,\n    configOverride: session.configOverride ?? undefined,\n    codexAttachOverride: deps.attachCommand,\n  }).command;\n  return fresh !== session.resolvedCommand && fresh.includes(attach);\n}\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
